  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district; basis recorded as cash. Receipts and disbursements from Exhibit D Total Major Governmental Funds column (p4); fund balances beginning 5,255,006 and ending 5,385,834 used as beginning/ending cash. Local Sources split into categories using the General, Nutrition, Activities, Depreciation and Special Building fund schedules (pp5, 7-10); the split items add to 5,650,271. County Sources split from General Fund 2110/2210. Operation and Maintenance of Plant split by fund column (General 1,181,213 support services; Depreciation 197,691 and Special Building 500,702 capital outlay). Debt Services split into General 98,977 (principal/interest not split) and Special Building 41,558. Transfers 360,000 in and out tie (General to Nutrition 90,000, Activities 70,000, Depreciation 200,000). Other financing = sale of property 17,002 + insurance proceeds 2,264. Balance sheet from Exhibit A (p1, government-wide modified cash). No business-type funds (School Nutrition is a special revenue fund here). Exhibit F total receipts 9,236,523 includes sale of property/insurance/other that Exhibit D reports as other financing or other. Detail covers every fund schedule once; the Exhibit F General Fund is by function only (not itemized by object). Roll-forward: 5,255,006 + 10,259,374 - 10,147,812 + 360,000 - 360,000 + 19,266 = 5,385,834. Read pages 1-10 of 10",
